{"step_index":497,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:27:53Z","thinking":"**Verifying graph connectivity constraint**\n\nThe SAT output appears valid, but a quick check reveals the generated graph is disconnected. Specifically, vertex 0 has no edges. The Z3 script did not enforce connectivity. The `HasRadius` condition, which uses `ballWithin`, seems appropriate to enforce graph connectivity.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\nfrom z3 import *\nimport sys\n\ndef search_counterexample(n, W):\n    s = Solver()\n    # Adjacency\n    adj = [[Bool(f\"adj_{i}_{j}\") for j in range(n)] for i in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        s.add(Not(adj[i][i]))\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            s.add(adj[i][j] == adj[j][i])\n    \n    # Distance bounds: reach[k][i][j]\n    # We need reach up to max(W, n)\n    max_k = max(W, n)\n    reach = [[[Bool(f\"r_{k}_{i}_{j}\") for j in range(n)] for i in range(n)] for k in range(max_k+1)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            if i == j:\n                s.add(reach[0][i][j])\n            else:\n                s.add(Not(reach[0][i][j]))\n    \n    for k in range(max_k):\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(n):\n                step = Or([And(reach[k][i][m], adj[m][j]) for m in range(n)])\n                s.add(reach[k+1][i][j] == Or(reach[k][i][j], step))\n    \n    # Condition: CONNECTED (HasRadius)\n    # reach[n-1][i][j] is True for all i, j\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            s.add(reach[n-1][i][j])\n            \n    # Condition 1: rad(G) >= W\n    # For every vertex i, there exists j such that dist(i, j) >= W (i.e. Not(reach[W-1][i][j]))\n    for i in range(n):\n        s.add(Or([Not(reach[W-1][i][j]) for j in range(n)]))\n    \n    # Condition 3: Exists Roman dominating function f with weight <= W\n    f = [Int(f\"f_{i}\") for i in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        s.add(Or(f[i] == 0, f[i] == 1, f[i] == 2))\n        dom = Or([And(adj[i][j], f[j] == 2) for j in range(n)])\n        s.add(Implies(f[i] == 0, dom))\n    \n    s.add(Sum(f) <= W)\n    \n    res = s.check()\n    if res == sat:\n        m = s.model()\n        edges = []\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i+1, n):\n                if is_true(m[adj[i][j]]):\n                    edges.append((i, j))\n        f_vals = [m[f[i]].as_long() for i in range(n)]\n        print(f\"SAT for n={n}, W={W}! edges={edges}, f={f_vals}\")\n        return True\n    else:\n        print(f\"UNSAT for n={n}, W={W}\")\n        return False\n\nprint(\"Running connected Z3 for W=2, 3, 4, 5, 6...\")\nfor W in [2, 3, 4, 5, 6]:\n    for n in range(W+1, 12):\n        if search_counterexample(n, W):\n            print(f\"FOUND COUNTEREXAMPLE at n={n}, W={W}!\")\n            sys.exit(0)\nprint(\"All UNSAT!\")\n'","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Running connected Z3 search","toolSummary":"Run connected Z3 search"}}]}
